From 018894e2ee3152563729901c4209896c24ff7bc4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sijie52 <sijie5452@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 09:58:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(c): preprocess by compile configuration instead of one
 macro table per file

- MacroEnvironment scans the translation unit and its headers line by line
  like a preprocessor: #define/#undef take effect from their position, each
  macro keeps a timeline of possible definitions, and a use site only sees
  the definitions in effect there (no expansion before the definition,
  #undef restores the plain call, redefinition wins).
- #if/#ifdef/#elif are evaluated three-valued under an explicit config
  (defines, undefines, target platform, unknownMacros cover|undefined).
  Lines of excluded branches are blanked before tree-sitter parses (offsets
  unchanged); undecided branches are kept, their definitions are marked
  _meta.conditional, and a macro with several possible definitions expands
  to a choice on __preprocessor_choice__ so each is analyzed.
- #include resolves headers through opts.preprocessor.resolveInclude; header
  macros take effect at the #include and CompileUnit._meta.includes lists
  the headers for per-translation-unit linkage.
- Replaces collectMacros, which kept the first non-Windows definition of a
  name for the whole file.
